rcheevos -- the RetroAchievements runtime (MIT, LICENSE beside this file).

Source:  https://github.com/RetroAchievements/rcheevos
Release: v12.5.0 (2026-09-13), commit 1433173220a7eaede6a9ed7a18e94117be1821e0
Taken:   2026-10-23.

Checked 2026-11-06 against upstream develop (eea6461, 29 commits after the
release; v12.5.0 is still the newest tag).  Develop is not taken whole: it
moves the source tree, renames the API (softcore -> casual, core/unofficial ->
promoted/unpromoted) and is unreleased.  Server requests are unchanged apart
from an optional "v=2" flag for unpromoted leaderboards, so v12.5.0 keeps
working with the RetroAchievements server.  Backported by hand, each marked
by its upstream commit in the log below:
  - 6d897b4  more than 65535 memrefs no longer wraps the 16-bit capacity
             (src/rcheevos/alloc.c)
  - 918ba6d  user-agent clause: no write past the buffer (src/rc_client.c)
  - 8409479  JSON: a null where a text is required is an error, nesting is
             limited to 32 levels, a deleted author/title no longer fails the
             whole answer (src/rapi/rc_api_common.c/.h, rc_api_info.c,
             rc_api_runtime.c; the editor API is not built here)
  - 8ffa4bc  challenge sets are no longer reported as bonus sets
             (rc_api_runtime.c, include/rc_api_runtime.h)
  - e9a6d58  progress loading is bounded to each chunk
             (src/rcheevos/runtime_progress.c)
  - 284de96  keeps unlock times in encore mode (src/rc_client.c; the app does
             not use encore mode; the field is unlock_time_softcore here)
  - db8ca2e  null checks in rc_client (develop, 2026-10-30, "add null checks to
             rc_client functions"; a local patch on v12.5.0, 2026-11-12): the
             award callback's mastery scan is in a helper that returns when
             client->game is NULL; failed allocations in the achievement and
             leaderboard lists and the game-hash list are returned, not used;
             a NULL display name counts as length 0; the hash-array sizes and
             the start-session error order follow upstream (src/rc_client.c).
             Upstream's diff names src/client/rc_client_*.c; here those four
             files are one src/rc_client.c, so the hunks were applied there,
             with the award-callback hunk and the game-hash hunk adapted by
             hand (the mastery code is not the same in the two layouts).
Not taken: 'rich presence lookup tree' balancing (cab7f7f, only speeds up
huge lookups), 'survive a failed allocation' (e3e7e86, needs the new source
layout), the restructure/rebranding/API-rename commits, hashes for consoles
this app does not load, and the disc-hash bounds checks (the disc hashers are
not built).

The files here are the release's, with the changes above, minus what VitAdhoc does not
build: the editor and RAIntegration APIs, the disc/zip/encrypted hashers
(a GB/GBC/GBA game's hash is the MD5 of its file, made by ra_vita.c with
md5.c), and the tests, the standalone validator tool and the project files.

Built with RC_NO_THREADS: the client is only ever called from the game's
thread (vita/ra_vita.c delivers the server's answers there).
